WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:03.467
The scrimmage against the Swallows was an away game.

2
00:00:03.468 --> 00:00:09.361
"I'm ready," Patrick repeated under his breath. But he hadn't gotten much sleep the night before.

3
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:14.737
His math quiz with a red 57 had sat on his desk like a warning light.

4
00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:18.124
And he'd been worried about who would start as catcher today.

5
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:24.425
Patrick rubbed his lucky catcher's mitt as Coach slapped the roster on the dugout wall. "Here's

6
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:27.895
the lineup, boys. Ready to play baseball?" "Yeah!"

7
00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:30.375
roared the team. Patrick

8
00:00:30.376 --> 00:00:36.589
took a deep breath and went over to look at the roster. Second

9
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.673
up for bat, Patrick Deboe, Number 12. Dell

10
00:00:40.674 --> 00:00:46.900
flashed him a grin. "Mickey's good. But you and I have got the dance down." Patrick

11
00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.714
grinned too. He

12
00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:56.155
and Dell were good dance partners, meaning that as pitcher and catcher, they could follow each other's moves instinctively. "Play

13
00:00:56.156 --> 00:01:01.757
ball!" the umpire yelled a few minutes later. The

14
00:01:01.758 --> 00:01:08.328
Dragons were up first. Patrick managed to hit a single. But

15
00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:12.571
the next three batters struck out, so the Dragons went scoreless. Dell

16
00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:20.222
headed to the mound while Patrick took his position behind home plate. "First game.

17
00:01:20.223 --> 00:01:28.459
First pitch," he thought happily. Mickey was a nice guy, but beating him for the starter position sure felt sweet. Now he

18
00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.116
had to prove he deserved to keep the position. The first

19
00:01:32.117 --> 00:01:35.545
batter up for the other team was Number 14. Patrick remembered

20
00:01:35.546 --> 00:01:39.711
that this batter was the one who crowded the plate. Patrick put

21
00:01:39.712 --> 00:01:47.524
down one finger to signal a fast pitch. Dell wound up and whizzed it in. "Strike!" called

22
00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:50.379
the umpire. Patrick nodded

23
00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:56.791
at Dell. Two more pitches, two more strikes, and they had their first out. "Nice work,

24
00:01:56.792 --> 00:01:59.714
you two!" called Daniel. "Finally, a

25
00:01:59.715 --> 00:02:03.528
compliment from Daniel!" Patrick thought. Number 42

26
00:02:03.529 --> 00:02:10.106
tapped his cleats with the bat and planted his feet in the dirt. Patrick remembered that

27
00:02:10.107 --> 00:02:17.104
this kid was a good hitter. He put down two fingers to signal a curve ball to Dell. Swoosh. "Strike!" The

28
00:02:17.105 --> 00:02:19.072
batter

29
00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:20.738
caught

30
00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:27.505
a piece of the next pitch, but the ball went foul. Patrick caught it easily. Patrick grinned. They

31
00:02:27.506 --> 00:02:31.671
had two outs already. * * *

32
00:02:31.672 --> 00:02:35.445
In middle school baseball, the teams played seven innings.

33
00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:40.075
By the bottom of the final inning, the Dragons were ahead, 7-6.

34
00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:43.138
Number 42 for the Swallows was up again.

35
00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.336
"He looks ready to slam a homerun," thought Patrick.

36
00:02:47.337 --> 00:02:49.535
He signaled Dell for the changeup.

37
00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:54.986
Dell's pitch was high, but Number 42 hit it solidly.

38
00:02:54.987 --> 00:03:03.219
The ball sailed just inside third base. In left field Todd dove for it.

39
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:10.028
Patrick held his breath as Todd rolled on the field. Would Todd come up with it? "Yes!"

40
00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:15.988
screamed Patrick, seeing Todd’s glove firmly wrapped around the ball. Two

41
00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:20.127
outs! One more out and the Dragons would win! Then

42
00:03:20.128 --> 00:03:25.675
everyone got quiet—Todd was still lying on the field. "Oh

43
00:03:25.676 --> 00:03:29.025
no," Patrick thought. Coach

44
00:03:29.026 --> 00:03:33.635
jogged out to check Todd's injury. Minutes

45
00:03:33.636 --> 00:03:40.527
later Todd stood, gingerly holding his arm against his chest. The

46
00:03:40.528 --> 00:03:47.749
crowd clapped as he walked off the field with Coach and over to his parents. Coach

47
00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:53.280
hurried over to the dugout and motioned for Mickey. Then he looked at Patrick. "Take

48
00:03:53.281 --> 00:04:00.946
left field, Patrick. This next batter hits deep, so we need someone with experience. Mickey will go in as catcher." "Okay,

49
00:04:00.947 --> 00:04:08.178
Coach," Patrick mumbled. He pulled off his catcher equipment and found his glove. As he

50
00:04:08.179 --> 00:04:12.087
put on his cap, he glanced at the Swallows' next batter. This kid

51
00:04:12.088 --> 00:04:16.015
liked the pitches low. Should he warn Mickey? "Nah. That's

52
00:04:16.016 --> 00:04:20.159
Daniel's job," thought Patrick. Dell's first

53
00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:26.655
pitch was a strike. Then a wild pitch from Dell put the Swallows batter on base. "That wasn't

54
00:04:26.656 --> 00:04:34.314
Mickey's fault," Patrick thought. But still the catcher always took the blame. It was just part of the job. The next

55
00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:38.742
batter had a chance to bring in the runner and tie up the score. Dell sent

56
00:04:38.743 --> 00:04:45.161
the pitch in, low and outside. The batter swung. The ball

57
00:04:45.162 --> 00:04:52.986
popped up behind home plate. Mickey scrambled to catch it, pulling off his mask. The ball drifted

58
00:04:52.987 --> 00:04:58.127
near the fence and then fell down, down . . . Mickey stretched over

59
00:04:58.128 --> 00:05:05.880
the fence, teetering to keep his balance. The ball settled solidly into his mitt. "Out!" cried the

60
00:05:05.881 --> 00:05:11.109
umpire. "Game over!" The Dragons had

61
00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:18.100
won! The team swarmed around home plate to congratulate Mickey. "What an amazing

62
00:05:18.101 --> 00:05:22.541
catch!" Patrick clapped Mickey on the back. "Thanks." Mickey grinned.

63
00:05:22.542 --> 00:05:28.269
"Another inch outside the fence and I wouldn't have reached it." The two of

64
00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:34.347
them joined the line to shake hands with the other team. Patrick tapped the

65
00:05:34.348 --> 00:05:40.108
hand of the Swallows player who had made the last out, feeling sorry for the guy. It was bad

66
00:05:40.109 --> 00:05:43.275
luck to be the hitter who made the last out. In the dugout everyone

67
00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:47.347
kept raving about Mickey's catch. Patrick was glad his

68
00:05:47.348 --> 00:05:53.011
team had won, but he felt a little jealous that he had missed the main action. "It's just one game,"

69
00:05:53.012 --> 00:06:00.843
he told himself. "Next time you'll be back where you belong—behind home plate." * * * "Huh?"

70
00:06:00.844 --> 00:06:04.174
Patrick said the next morning at school. Dell

71
00:06:04.175 --> 00:06:10.657
repeated the bad news. "Todd injured his shoulder. He's out for at least a week." "He

72
00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:14.720
can't play against the Bandits?" asked Patrick. Patrick

73
00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:20.563
had already started memorizing the Bandits' roster, the first team on the Dragons' regular schedule. "Nope."

74
00:06:20.564 --> 00:06:26.975
Dell looked grim. "And it will be a challenge to beat them without our star hitter." "You're

75
00:06:26.976 --> 00:06:33.308
right," Patrick agreed. "And . . ." His heart sank at another realization. "Mickey is

76
00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:38.273
a good hitter. Coach will probably start him as catcher." "Yep. In

77
00:06:38.274 --> 00:06:44.787
three weeks we play the Hornets—our biggest rivals. I hope Todd's back by then." Patrick nodded.

78
00:06:44.788 --> 00:06:48.934
He hoped Todd would be back by then too. * *

79
00:06:48.935 --> 00:06:53.526
* The weather for practice after school was cold and

80
00:06:53.527 --> 00:06:58.277
dreary. Patrick worked with the fielders while Daniel spent extra time coaching

81
00:06:58.278 --> 00:07:02.106
Mickey. Patrick couldn't help glancing toward home plate a few

82
00:07:02.107 --> 00:07:07.359
times. "Way to go, Mickey!" Daniel kept saying. "You're framing pitches really

83
00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:12.276
well." Just then a ball thrown by the center fielder sailed past

84
00:07:12.277 --> 00:07:18.680
Patrick. "Patrick!" snapped Coach. "Are you picking dandelions out there? Where's your

85
00:07:18.681 --> 00:07:24.766
head?" "Sorry," muttered Patrick. He ran to retrieve the ball.

86
00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:27.734
"Pay attention!" he scolded himself.

87
00:07:27.735 --> 00:07:33.601
If he wasn't careful, he'd be sitting on the bench during games, with most of the other seventh-graders.

88
00:07:33.602 --> 00:07:41.990
Finally rain forced Coach to shorten practice. For once Patrick didn't mind going home early.

89
00:07:41.991 --> 00:07:54.863
He needed to study. His grade on the last math quiz had been better—but it wasn't good enough to satisfy his mother.

